{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote"]]},"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The notehead type indicates shapes other than the open and closed ovals associated with note durations."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Notehead"}],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The smufl attribute can be used to specify a particular notehead, allowing application interoperability","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"without requiring every SMuFL glyph to have a MusicXML element equivalent. This attribute can be used either","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with the “other” value, or to refine a specific notehead value such as “cluster”. Noteheads in the SMuFL Note","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"name noteheads and Note name noteheads supplement ranges (U+E150–U+E1AF and U+EEE0–U+EEFF) should not use the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"smufl attribute or the “other” value, but instead use the notehead-text element.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"For the enclosed shapes, the default is to be hollow for half notes and longer, and filled otherwise. The","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"filled attribute can be set to change this if needed.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"If the parentheses attribute is set to yes, the notehead is parenthesized. It is no by default.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Maps the MusicXML ","type":"text"},{"code":"<notehead>","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" element.","type":"text"}],"type":"